<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amuq Valley</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Amuq plain</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Amuq Valley is a fertile plain in Hatay province, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, around the lower Orontes near Antakya. It was densely settled from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neolithic">Neolithic</a> onwards, and its mounds include <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alalakh">Alalakh</a>, capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> kingdom of Mukish, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-tayinat">Tell Tayinat</a>, capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> kingdom of Patina. A lake in its centre was drained in the 20th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amuq-valley.jpg" alt="Amuq Valley" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Radyokid at Turkish Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amik_Ovas%C4%B1%27n%C4%B1n_Amanoslar%27dan_g%C3%B6r%C3%BCn%C3%BCm%C3%BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
